Subject: Backport array_first()/array_last() instead of vendoring symfony/polyfill-php85

Upstream's composer.json requires symfony/polyfill-php85, which is not
packaged in Debian (checked: absent from trixie, sid, and backports).
This is a real dependency, not a version-floor nicety: array_first()/
array_last() (added to PHP itself in 8.5) are called at 30+ sites across
program/lib and program/include, and trixie's PHP is 8.4.

Rather than package the whole polyfill library or vendor it via a
separate composer install, this is a direct backport: the two functions
Roundcube actually calls are reimplemented in program/include/iniset.php
(the single bootstrap shared by both the web and CLI entry points, see
program/include/clisetup.php), ported verbatim from that package's
Php85.php, guarded by function_exists() and PHP_VERSION_ID < 80500 so it
becomes a no-op once trixie eventually ships PHP >= 8.5.

This is judged low-risk because the ported implementation is small,
directly comparable line-by-line to upstream's polyfill source, and
guarded to only ever run on exactly the PHP versions upstream's own
polyfill would have covered.

Forwarded: not-needed
---
Index: rc-build/composer.json
===================================================================
--- rc-build.orig/composer.json
+++ rc-build/composer.json
@@ -16,8 +16,7 @@
         "pear/net_smtp": "~1.12.0",
         "pear/pear-core-minimal": "~1.10.15",
         "roundcube/plugin-installer": "~0.3.5",
-        "roundcube/rtf-html-php": "^2.1",
-        "symfony/polyfill-php85": "^1.33.0"
+        "roundcube/rtf-html-php": "^2.1"
     },
     "require-dev": {
         "ergebnis/composer-normalize": "^2.13",
Index: rc-build/program/include/iniset.php
===================================================================
--- rc-build.orig/program/include/iniset.php
+++ rc-build/program/include/iniset.php
@@ -26,6 +26,30 @@ if (\PHP_VERSION_ID < 80100) {
     exit('Unsupported PHP version. Required PHP >= 8.1.');
 }
 
+// Backport of array_first()/array_last(), added to PHP in 8.5. Debian doesn't
+// package symfony/polyfill-php85, so the two functions this codebase actually
+// uses from it are reimplemented here directly (ported from that package's
+// Php85.php, which Roundcube's own composer.json requires).
+if (\PHP_VERSION_ID < 80500) {
+    if (!function_exists('array_first')) {
+        function array_first(array $array)
+        {
+            foreach ($array as $value) {
+                return $value;
+            }
+
+            return null;
+        }
+    }
+
+    if (!function_exists('array_last')) {
+        function array_last(array $array)
+        {
+            return $array ? current(array_slice($array, -1)) : null;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
 // application constants
 define('RCMAIL_VERSION', '1.7-git');
 define('RCMAIL_START', microtime(true));
